cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use origami, please cite it using the metadata below, and cite the papers of the models you use."
type: software
title: "origami: compare foundation-model embeddings, hand-crafted and catalogue features of astronomical light curves"
abstract: >-
  origami compares representations of astronomical light curves under identical
  conditions: embeddings from frozen time-series foundation models, hand-crafted
  features and catalogue columns, evaluated on the same objects, epochs, folds
  and probes, for regression, classification, clustering and anomaly detection.
authors:
  - family-names: Monti
    given-names: Lorenzo
    affiliation: "INAF – Osservatorio di Astrofisica e Scienza dello Spazio di Bologna"
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-10-23
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/LorenzoMonti/origami"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/origami-astro/"
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - light curves
  - time series
  - foundation models
  - embeddings
  - benchmark
